from pathlib import Path
import json,base64,html,hashlib,platform,importlib.metadata
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;O=R/'results';OUT=R.parent/'output'
stats=json.load((O/'coverage.json').open());combined=json.load((O/'combined_summary.json').open());emb=json.load((O/'embedding_assessment.json').open());sh=json.load((O/'shacl_summary.json').open())
def table(headers,rows):return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+html.escape(h)+'</th>' for h in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+html.escape(str(c))+'</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
parts=['''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>CNP knowledge graph and skill experiment</title><style>body{font:17px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif;color:#17313d;background:#f6f4ee;margin:0}main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:48px 30px}h1{font-size:38px;line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:27px;margin-top:42px;color:#006f73}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px;margin:24px 0}th,td{padding:12px 16px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #cdd7d7;vertical-align:top}th{background:#006f73;color:white}tbody tr:nth-child(odd){background:white}code,pre{font-family:ui-monospace,monospace;font-size:14px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:white;padding:20px}img{width:100%;height:auto}a{color:#006f73}.note{border-left:4px solid #b6502b;padding:10px 18px;background:#fff}small{color:#52616a}li{margin:10px 0}@media print{main{padding:0}h2{break-after:avoid}table{break-inside:avoid}}</style><main><small>ReproNim symposium worked experiment · 14 October 2026</small><h1>A dataset, its papers, and a testable agent procedure</h1><p>This experiment turns the skills section into a concrete scientific workflow. It builds a NIDM/PROV graph from the pinned ds000030 phenotype tables, connects selected paper claims to research questions and evidence, executes a bounded StructSense extraction, and derives a participant UMAP from graph queries.</p><p class="note"><strong>Scope:</strong> complete coverage of the pinned phenotype tables, plus MRI inventory and selected acquisition metadata. This is not a complete raw-image-to-publication provenance reconstruction. Missing links remain explicit.</p>''']
parts.append('<h2>1. What the dataset graph contains</h2>')
parts.append(table(['Aspect','Observed coverage'],[['Pinned dataset commit','4070b6eea231517bfeff42527a46d9d166ac4e13'],['Participants','272'],['Phenotype tables / dictionaries','52 / 52'],['Table columns','1,983; all have dictionary entries'],['Participant-table records','14,144'],['Observed / missing cells','411,584 / 127,792'],['MRI file inventory','2,531 pointers: 265 T1w, 262 DWI, 2,004 BOLD'],['Combined RDF graph',f"{combined['triples']:,} triples"],['Integrity','No duplicate table participant IDs or unknown participant IDs']]))
parts.append('''<p>Triple count measures representation size, not scientific completeness. The dictionary files contain one additional entry beyond the table columns. Raw observed values remain source strings. Missing values have explicit missing-variable edges, and the original TSVs retain their exact sentinels. The embedding pipeline performs numeric conversion separately.</p>''')
parts.append(table(['Scientific object','Graph representation','Concrete relation'],[['Participant','prov:Person / prov:Agent','Acquisition associates the participant through a Subject role'],['Visit container','nidm:Session / prov:Activity','dct:isPartOf the Project'],['Scan or questionnaire','nidm:Acquisition / prov:Activity','AcquisitionObject prov:wasGeneratedBy Acquisition'],['Measured variable','nidm:DataElement / prov:Entity','Definition includes original variable name and dictionary provenance'],['Observed record','nidm:AcquisitionObject / prov:Entity','DataElement URI acts as predicate; raw value is its literal'],['Derived measurement','nidm:DerivativeObject','wasGeneratedBy processing; wasDerivedFrom source record'],['Processing','nidm:Derivative / prov:Activity','prov:used source and wasAssociatedWith software']]))
parts.append('''<p>Mappings follow the retrieved <a href="https://github.com/incf-nidash/PyNIDM/blob/master/src/nidm/experiment/schema/nidm_schema.yaml">PyNIDM experiment schema</a>. The graph explicitly labels reconstructed acquisition/session containers. Their dates and historical execution identities are unknown. Local terms describe evidence status, missingness and claim/question relationships; they are not presented as NIDM standards.</p><h2>2. A source-to-derivative chain that was tested</h2><p>The Barratt dictionary defines <code>bis_parcel1</code> as the mean of items 19 and 17. For sub-10159 the source items are 2 and 2, yielding 2.0. Recomputing this formula matches the recorded value for <strong>272 of 272 participants</strong>. The graph links each newly computed output to its computation and input record. The formula names the exact input columns.</p><p>This validates one behavioral derivation. It does not validate every variable marked as a derivative, and it does not prove the original historical software used this same execution.</p><h2>3. Connecting behavior to image-derived phenotypes</h2><p>A participant can connect a behavioral record to an imaging derivative. A usable imaging record must specify the measure, brain region, laterality, atlas/version, units, processing software/version, QC status and source imaging artifact. A visit or time-point link is necessary when repeated measures are possible.</p>''')
parts.append(table(['Potential research question','Required graph join','Important qualification'],[['Is response inhibition associated with regional cortical thickness?','Participant → SSRT record; same participant → thickness derivative → T1 image','Confirm SSRT units, atlas, laterality and temporal alignment'],['Does a behavioral association survive pipeline changes?','Same source image → two named pipelines → comparable regional measures','Keep QC and processing alternatives distinct'],['Do connectivity features add information beyond behavior?','Participant → cognitive scores and rsFC features → fold-specific model','Prevent preprocessing/feature-selection leakage across folds']]))
parts.append('''<p class="note">Participant FreeSurfer stats and processing logs were not retrieved. Public derivative requests failed in this runtime. No participant imaging measurements or verified historical image-source links were invented. These proposed joins become executable only after importing the actual artifacts and checking their provenance.</p><h2>4. A real phenotype UMAP</h2><p>The matrix comes from a SPARQL projection of the graph. It contains 272 participants and 10 prespecified behavioral/cognitive scores: three Barratt second-order scores, three WAIS raw scores, quantile SSRT, ANT reaction-time conflict effect, CPT hits and CPT false alarms. Columns and participants needed at least 80% coverage/completeness. All selected participants and features passed; three missing cells were median-imputed. Columns were then standardized.</p><p>Diagnosis, age, sex and scanner were excluded from the inputs. UMAP used Euclidean distance, 15 neighbors, minimum distance 0.1, 500 epochs, and seeded random state 42 in the pinned UMAP-JS implementation. Diagnosis only colors the points.</p>''')
parts.append('<img alt="UMAP by diagnosis and age, with PCA comparison" src="data:image/png;base64,'+base64.b64encode((O/'phenotype_embedding.png').read_bytes()).decode()+'">')
parts.append(table(['Sensitivity check','Observed result'],[['UMAP trustworthiness, 15 neighbors','0.8739'],['Same input matrix, PCA in two dimensions','0.8047'],['UMAP seeds 43 / 44','Trustworthiness 0.8676 / 0.8793'],['Neighbor overlap with seed 42','0.7358 / 0.7382'],['UMAP with 30 neighbors','Trustworthiness 0.8669; overlap 0.7206']]))
parts.append('''<p>Trustworthiness measures preservation of local neighborhoods in the original matrix. It does not validate diagnostic clusters. The graph makes selection and provenance inspectable; it is not necessary for UMAP mathematically and does not itself improve the embedding. Correlated score weighting, demographics and scanner sensitivity deserve further analysis. No diagnostic or causal inference was tested.</p><h2>5. Questions, claims, and evidence</h2>''')
parts.append(table(['Paper','Question or purpose','What the evidence resolves'],[['Poldrack 2016','Create a resource for dimensional neurocognitive investigation across diagnostic groups','Enables research; a data descriptor does not settle all biological questions'],['Gorgolewski 2017','Provide reusable preprocessing and quality-control outputs','Reports a processing resource; per-file historical provenance still needs inspection'],['Kim 2023','Does increased connectivity add predictive information, and do features transfer?','Conditional within-dataset support; transfer is direction-dependent']]))
parts.append('''<p>In Kim 2023, the graph attaches the reported 70.2% result to UCLA leave-one-out evaluation using both connectivity directions. Decreased-connectivity features yield 61.5% when training on UCLA and testing on COBRE. Reverse transfer does not predict above chance. These support a narrower conclusion than universal generalization or a causal mechanism. Questions here are curator formulations of the papers’ aims; numeric results are author reports.</p><p>The chain is <strong>question → claim → evaluation → cohort/model → dataset</strong>. Exact participant membership and per-file processing provenance remain unresolved. Sharing ds000030 does not establish use of the 2017 derivatives: the later paper reports GRETNA/SPM12.</p><h2>6. The executed skill test</h2><p>The pilot uses <a href="https://github.com/sensein/agent_skills/tree/dde54251a5a70f55d0b9bbbaab0dd21013b1bbfc/skills/structsense">StructSense 0.12.0</a>, pinned to commit <code>dde54251…</code>. It follows the structured-extraction reference and prompt, with a schema derived from the requested claim, evidence and scope fields. The host model authored six bounded records. The upstream <code>span_validator.py</code> ran unchanged. Ajv checked JSON Schema. Explicit vocabulary lookup and source review supplied alignment and faithfulness judgments.</p><p>This is a structured-mode subset, not an exhaustive extraction or a complete run of the NER/resource pipeline. The same host model performed review; it is procedurally separate, not an independent model assessment. Exact backend model identifier was unavailable.</p>''')
parts.append(table(['Executed check','Result'],[['Six exact evidence spans','6 / 6 pass'],['JSON Schema','Pass; wrong numeric type rejected'],['Wrong offsets','Repair succeeds and marks span_repaired'],['Invented evidence phrase','Dropped by the upstream span validator'],['Combined graph SHACL profile','Pass'],['Remove a derivative source edge','Rejected'],['Keep the numeric span but invent a causal interpretation','Span gate still passes; scientific interpretation is unsupported']]))
parts.append('''<p>The last test is the most instructive. An exact quotation and a well-formed graph can coexist with a false interpretation. Schema, lexical grounding, ontology existence and scientific entailment are different checks.</p><h2>7. Validating the skill versus validating an output</h2>''')
parts.append(table(['Skill itself','One output'],[['Freeze skill, prompt, schema and dependency versions','Record exact input hashes, source locators and execution parameters'],['Use held-out documents with independently curated gold annotations','Check this output’s schema and evidence spans'],['Measure claim/relation precision, recall, scope errors and appropriate abstention','Review entailment, cohort scope, units, uncertainty and negation'],['Test adversarial inputs, repeatability, cost and recovery','Check graph constraints, joins and dangling references'],['Retest changes across document types and models','Recompute derivatives; inspect image-specific scientific QC']]))
parts.append('''<p>Current evidence establishes bounded smoke tests and specific failure demonstrations. It does not establish skill-wide precision/recall, calibrated confidence or autonomous scientific reliability. SHACL checks a local six-shape NIDM/PROV profile, not all possible NIDM rules or the scientific truth of every triple.</p><h2>8. Does the graph improve on LLM search?</h2><p>The executed graph queries return exact participant counts, variable counts, a derivative’s provenance chain, a transfer claim and its qualifying evidence. The original inventory join returns 261 participants with both T1w and resting BOLD. Such joins, completeness checks, stable identifiers and explicit counterevidence are useful graph capabilities. Search is useful for discovery and interpretation. An agent with equivalent tables, code and constraints may perform just as well without RDF.</p><p><strong>No controlled LLM-only versus graph-assisted performance experiment was run.</strong> A fair evaluation would compare search only, skill only, graph only and both, with the same corpus, model, tools and budget. Include a SQL/table baseline, independent gold answers, repeated trials, graph-construction cost and errors introduced during extraction. Score correctness, evidence completeness, unsupported claims, abstention, latency and cost.</p><h2>9. A harness for reducing agent drift</h2><p>The skill describes the procedure. The graph supplies persistent, versioned scientific state. The execution harness must enforce transitions: propose a change set, validate in a staging graph, review semantic changes, then promote accepted changes with a recorded graph diff. Pin input, skill, schema, prompt and software versions. Keep reported findings distinct from independently reproduced findings.</p>''')
parts.append(table(['Drift type','Concrete control','Evidence here'],[['Source/version drift','Reject unapproved manifest changes','Architecture specified; no long-session experiment'],['Provenance drift','Require derivative source links','Missing-source mutation rejected'],['Scope drift','Require evaluation, cohort and evidence status','Scoped records built; semantic drift not comprehensively tested'],['Interpretation drift','Independent source review and scientific tests','Causal-overclaim counterexample shows lexical gate limitation'],['Analysis drift','Preserve features, preprocessing, seeds and output hashes','UMAP provenance and sensitivity outputs recorded']]))
parts.append('''<p>The graph can make drift detectable and reviewable. It cannot guarantee its prevention, and this pilot does not measure a reduction in long-horizon agent drift.</p><h2>10. Reuse and next evidence</h2><p>The accompanying ZIP contains the combined Turtle graph, NIDM and claim components, all pinned phenotype metadata, source hashes, extraction records, validation reports, executable queries, UMAP coordinates and analysis code. The presentation has 25 main slides and 17 backup slides. The most valuable next acquisition is participant-level FreeSurfer stats plus logs and source manifests, followed by the exact paper cohort manifest. A controlled agent ablation should follow independently reviewed ground truth.</p><p>Primary sources: <a href="https://github.com/OpenNeuroDatasets/ds000030/tree/4070b6eea231517bfeff42527a46d9d166ac4e13">pinned ds000030</a>; <a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/sdata2016110">Poldrack 2016</a>; <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5664981/">Gorgolewski 2017</a>; <a href="https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2023.1232015/full">Kim 2023</a>; <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/">PROV-O</a>; <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/">SHACL</a>; <a href="https://github.com/PAIR-code/umap-js/tree/14abb51c523f71456550a7c6ef3f7062127b6bad">UMAP-JS</a>.</p></main></html>''')
(OUT/'CNP_Knowledge_Graph_Experiment.html').write_text('\n'.join(parts))
manifest={'dataset_commit':'4070b6eea231517bfeff42527a46d9d166ac4e13','skill_commit':'dde54251a5a70f55d0b9bbbaab0dd21013b1bbfc','umap_commit':'14abb51c523f71456550a7c6ef3f7062127b6bad','python':platform.python_version(),'files':{}}
for root in [R/'data',R/'results',R/'vendor/structsense']:
 for p in sorted(root.rglob('*')):
  if p.is_file() and '__pycache__' not in str(p):manifest['files'][str(p.relative_to(R))]=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
